hi there steve here again we're week 8  of our 12 week 90 day challenge  and today i want to talk a little bit  about output in other words producing  the language now you know that  i believe along with stephen krashen  leading expert on language acquisition  that our  ability in the language will come  primarily from our input activities  listening and reading  occasional looking at grammar occasional  review of words and phrases perhaps a  focus on phrases all of this input  activity is building up our ability in  the language but all of us or most of us  want to be able to speak or write but  primarily speak and speak well so we  have to at some point start doing that  outputting the language  in the language now there are  opportunities that link that we have the  exchange where you can put text that you  start writing and have other members  correct them  and it is often easier to start writing  if you have the patience to write  because you have time to look things up  you have time to think about what you're  going to say obviously when you're  speaking you don't have so much time  so that's one place where you can start  but i think most of us  perhaps if i say  in my own case i'm a bit too lazy to  write i might write for example you can  write just even in your flashcards you  have that dictation function  where you hear it you have to write it  or you have  reverse flashcards where you have the  say english or whatever your native  language is and you have to produce it  in the target language but these are  minor things the main activity that we  kind of want to get into is speaking so  this means getting a tutor  and  where we have  tutors in those languages where we have  tutors that link i use our link tutors  where we don't have tutors  at link for some languages i have in the  past gone to italki but i prefer  to do it within link  i have good tutors for the languages  that i'm learning right now persian and  arabic  and the advantage is that we get a  report  with audio that we can listen to and so  here is the thing about our interaction  with the tutor  the interaction with the tutor is an  opportunity to speak of course you will  struggle  you will  simply not be able to remember words  that you thought you knew uh you'll make  mistakes in grammar that in fact you  know their mistakes almost even as  you're saying them incorrectly but you  just have to work your way through that  a good  tutor will give you a good list i get a  good list of the words and phrases that  i struggled with  and record them  and so this gives me then content that i  can review over and over again  and uh you know i might have 30 or 40 or  more of these conversation reports  in the languages that i've been learning  and so i can go back to a conversation  that i had six months ago and go over  some of those words and realize that in  fact i've already forgotten them and i  regularly do review so the output  activity  is not only an opportunity for you to  speak it's also an opportunity to create  more input activity than that you can  use because ultimately  the major sort of way in which you're  going to upgrade your language skills is  this commitment to ongoing  listening and reading input activities  increasing your vocabulary improving  your  comprehension skills this is the base  from which you will gradually develop  the ability to speak and the only way  you're going to speak better if you do  all of these other things is to speak  more  and that's going to mean more  interaction with your tutor or  if you have an opportunity wherever you  live as is the case with me in vancouver  there are a lot of persian speakers  where i live so if i go into a store  whether it be a persian grocery store or  even a department store and they have  staff there that are persian speakers  you can  you better believe that i'm going to  speak to them in persian  i didn't the level of my persian through  this 90-day challenge has improved to a  level where i can now engage with those  people so i'm certainly going to do that  and every time you do that  not only are you sort of discovering  where your gaps are which makes you more  alert when you listen and read  but it stimulates you it motivates you  and we all require motivation to stay on  task so  when it comes to output don't be  discouraged if you don't do as well as  you would like don't be discouraged if  you do well one time and do less well  the next time  i would also recommend that you focus a  lot of your listening activity and  reading activity on our mini stories  because i have found that they have  enabled me to start speaking much much  earlier because there is a lot of  repetition built around the most common  verbs in a language and we need to have  verbs in order to express our ideas  and in many languages the verbs create  have a lot of grammatical issues that  are difficult to get used to so i would  do a lot of listening and reading of the  many stories in preparation for  your output activities but ultimately  you have to get going don't second-guess  yourself just let it fly out of your  mouth  don't  try to remember the rules of grammar  just see rules of grammar see what  you're able to say  review your  conversation reports when you get them  back from your tutor  so go and explore the tutor section at  link look at who we have there that are  tutors in your language and see if you  can't find someone who is going to be to  your liking and if you don't like the  first one try another one so that's what  i have to say about output it's  two-thirds of the way through here  and it's time to start maybe doing a  little more output activity all right  thank you bye for now
 

